VALUES ('GLY-003', 'Pair carbohydrate with protein', 'glycemic', 'macro balance', 'carbohydrate-dominant meal', 'MACRO_CARB', 'postprandial glucose and satiety', 'OUT_PPG', 'Add an appropriate protein source', 'PAIR_PROTEIN_CARB', 'Protein can slow gastric emptying and stimulate insulin, blunting glucose excursion in some meals', 'Add beans, tofu, eggs, fish, poultry, yogurt, or another profile-compatible protein without excessive calories.', 'Insulin response may rise; kidney disease and protein prescriptions require clinical constraints.', 'general', 'B', 'Controlled mixed-meal studies support reduced glucose excursion, but responses differ by protein and metabolic status.', 'recipe_safe', 'Effect of protein ingestion on postprandial glucose responses', 'peer-reviewed review', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25926512/', '2026-09-17', TRUE)
